## TAF libraries and code workflow

**TAF** means **Test Automation Framework**: shared libraries used by testers and automation
code (Python helpers, Robot resources, and related glue). **UTE** TAF libraries are the
product-side namespaces commonly imported as `taf.namespaces.*` in test code.

## TAF library naming conventions

TAF libraries follow systematic naming schemes that reflect their generation, domain, and function. Understanding these conventions is essential for resolving imports, locating the right library, and distinguishing active from legacy code.

### Naming generations (prefix families)

| Prefix | Generation / context | Status tendency | Example |
|--------|---------------------|-----------------|---------|
| `taf.*` | Current canonical namespace — all modern libraries live here | `lead` / `active` | `taf.sbts.oam.coam.admin`, `taf.collectors.pmcounters` |
| `ta_*` | First-generation flat namespace (underscore-separated) | mostly `deprecated` | `ta_cell_operations`, `ta_commissioning` |
| `ta5g_*` | 5G-targeted generation of the flat `ta_*` libraries | `active` / `lead` | `ta5g_commissioning`, `ta5g_delta` |
| `taf.ul.*` | User-library sub-namespace for team-owned extensions | `active` / `lead` | `taf.ul.ettf`, `taf.ul.sc`, `taf.ul.oran_mplane` |
| `taf.rfrl.*` | RFRL-specific Robot Framework resource libraries | `active` | `taf.rfrl.bts`, `taf.rfrl.tm500` |
| `rfsw.*` | RF software domain libraries | `active` / `lead` | `rfsw.procemon`, `rfsw.qc.client` |

