### Library lifecycle statuses

| Status | Meaning | Recommended action |
|--------|---------|-------------------|
| `lead` | Current authoritative implementation, fully maintained | **Use this**; prefer over all others |
| `active` | Actively used and maintained; may lack full versioning | Use when `lead` equivalent does not exist |
| `deprecated` | Officially superseded; still callable but receives no new features; may get critical fixes only | Migrate to the `lead`/`active` replacement; do not use in new test code |
| `legacy` | Frozen, unmaintained code from a previous generation; kept only for backward compatibility | Do not use in new code; refactor existing usages to the current equivalent when possible |
